--
N5008 [dcl.spec.auto]/2-3 + [temp.variadic]/5.  A decltype(auto) function whose
body declares a LOCAL type alias and uses it to construct the argument of a
nested deduced-return call (`using Ind = seq<0,1>; return inner(Ind{});`) -- the
shape of std::apply's `using _Indices = ...; return __apply_impl(..., _Indices{});`.
Previously the return type could not be typed from the return expression in
isolation (the body-local alias was not yet in scope), so deduction was
deferred, and typecheck_return then tried to convert the return value to the
still-unresolved `<<type:decltype>>` and aborted.  Fixed by deducing a
decltype(auto) return type in typecheck_return without a conversion (as for
plain auto).  Covers a fixed and a dependent local alias.  Non-vacuous: each
result is a concrete function of the pack carried by the local alias.
